  "summary": "The hour Jesus asked of Peter passes for an adult parish assembly because the hearer of the warning in Mark 13:3\u20134, 33\u201337 becomes the friend found asleep in 14:29\u201340, giving a particular reason to keep the promised visit. The sentence \u201cFirst they ask God to give them life\u201d connects Psalm 80:19 with the Collect\u2019s request for the will to act, in accord with Isaiah 64:7, Jerome\u2019s Commentary on Isaiah XVII, pp. 158\u2013159, Augustine\u2019s Exposition on Psalm 79 \u00a7\u00a73, 11 and the reviewed study. The 1,121-word body runs about 10 minutes 40 seconds at the stated 105 words per minute, an estimate from the written text."
